    annotation={'schema':'riverstone.next_multiview_correspondence_annotation.v1','source_sha256':C['source_sha256'],'source_status':'approved_image_generated_turnaround','views':views,'alignment_observed_vs_assumed':{'observed':'Actual source pixels, measured class masks and color landmarks; guide/crown/sole positions are image coordinates.','manual':'View crops, axis_u and shared physical test height1.2m are explicit alignment annotations.','inferred':'Side yaw75deg is not measured/calibrated;60/90deg are comparison hypotheses. Orthographic projection and equal scale are assumptions.','limits':'No known focal length, physical stature, camera calibration or exact90degree side. Front/back axis and pose may be inconsistent.'},'regions':{'head_cap':{'identity':'same anatomical head/cap region across views','surface_point_correspondence':'unknown','masks':'hair positive plus observed face skin above annotated chin level; background negative; other foreground unknown'},'long_hair':{'identity':'same hairstyle class, not matched strand identity','individual_strands':'unknown; row-run path is explicitly rejected as proof of one physical strand','occlusion':'body/face/bouquet in front can hide hair; semantic-zero is not empty-space evidence'},'cloth':{'identity':'same costume class, sewn panel identities unknown','previous_front05_side01_pair':'vertical-extent score only, not physical correspondence evidence','required_next_annotation':'Mark visible fold/edge boundaries, occluding order, attachment search regions, candidate matched pieces or unknown. Never force full silhouette as one panel truth.'}},'visual_hull_interpretation':'Only an outer-envelope/support baseline. Multi-view silhouette intersection cannot recover concavities, interior strand gaps, layering, hidden sewing or face anatomy. Ternary masks avoid carving occluded hair as empty space.','next_steps':['Freeze ternary region masks and explicit camera/pose hypotheses before geometry.','Compare whole head/cap silhouette intersection across yaw hypotheses before any individual strand decomposition.','For long hair/cloth, record region-boundary candidates across views; keep unmatched boundaries unknown.','If no cross-view candidate is justified, retain an uncertainty volume rather than assign an arbitrary physical strand or thin garment.'],'new_3D_geometry_generated':False}
